## 7. Animation System & Audio

*Custom systems, not Godot's built-in animation tooling.*

### Milestone 7.1 — .lanim format + tooling
- [ ] Animator UI (Roblox Animator-style)
- [ ] Real-time animation-to-code conversion
- [ ] Animation smoother, toggleable for a retro/choppy look option
- [ ] Apply this animation system to non-character objects too
**Acceptance criteria:** A creator can key a simple animation in the Animator UI, export it as .lanim, and see it play correctly on a rigged character in-lot, with the smoother togglable.
**Difficulty:** 🔴 Animator UI · 🟠 real-time conversion · 🟡 smoother

### Milestone 7.2 — Audio system
- [ ] Sound playback/mixing, 3D positional audio, and an audio pool (no audio exists in the project today)
- [ ] Audio bound into the Lua API so scripts can play cues (verb-first methods per §2.2)
**Acceptance criteria:** A script can play a sound on an object and a player hears it positioned at that object in the lot.
**Difficulty:** 🔴 (nothing exists yet) · 🟠 Lua binding

### Milestone 7.3 — Sound service / audio emitters
- [ ] `SoundEmitter` — an **insertable object** (spawned from the Toolbox like a Capsule, §3.4) that plays a sound positioned in the 3D world with range/falloff, parented to whatever it is attached to so it moves with that object
- [ ] Built on §7.2's pool and mixer rather than a second playback path — the emitter is the object-facing front end of the pool the audio system already owns
- [ ] Per-emitter properties through the §2.3 `LotPropertyRegistry` (sound asset, volume, pitch, loop, 3D range/falloff, playing), so the Inspector and the Lua verbs come from one declaration per §2.2
- [ ] Fired from Lua (`PlaySound` / `StopSound` / `SetSoundVolume`, verb-first per §2.2) and from the §3.7 event system, so a `touched` handler can trigger a cue with no new plumbing
- [ ] Sound assets are the archive's `assets/` audio read through `LotVFS` (§4.1), and the emitter serializes in `lot.json` — a saved lot ships its sounds
- [ ] A cue other players must hear is fired through `net.server` (host-authoritative, §1.3); a purely local cue stays local — the same origination rule the rest of the runtime uses
**Acceptance criteria:** A script plays a sound on an emitter object and a player hears it positioned at that object with the emitter's range applied, and the same cue is still there after the lot is saved and reloaded.
**Difficulty:** 🟠 emitter object + property wiring · 🟠 Lua/event firing · 🟠 persistence (asset bytes via §4.1)

---

## 8. Networking

### Milestone 8.1 — Session model
- [ ] Host/join/list session model
- [ ] State sync across clients
- [ ] **Headless runtime bootstrapping:** a `--lot <path>` CLI flag starts a dedicated host that opens a `.lot` archive through `LotVFS` (§4.1), reads `manifest.json` for `maxPlayers` and the **entry script**, runs that script as the lot root, and joins the session model as host — **bypassing UI and rendering viewport nodes**: no ImGui/dockspace, no `ViewportWindow` / `SubViewport` / camera nodes are created; only physics, the `net.*` router and `ScriptRuntime.Tick` run. Composes with Godot's own `--headless` flag (no display server); the same binary is a player client when launched without `--lot`.
- [ ] Bind the transport through the existing **`INetTransport` seam** (`NetTransport.cs`), replacing `LoopbackTransport` for a networked session — the router and wire codec are already transport-agnostic, so a headless host and a client pick their transport by role rather than a hardcoded peer id (§8.2 rule)
**Acceptance criteria:** Two clients can join the same hosted lot and see each other's characters move in real time with acceptable sync; the same `.lot` can be started UI-less as a dedicated host via `--lot <path>` and accept a joining client.
**Difficulty:** 🔴 🔴 — highest-research items on the whole roadmap; budget real standalone research time here

### Milestone 8.2 — Decentralized/self-hosting model
- [ ] Peer-to-peer hosting path (free/default option, alongside Providers — see §13)
**Acceptance criteria:** A user can host a lot from their own machine and have it be joinable/discoverable without a Provider in the loop.
**Difficulty:** 🔴

### Milestone 8.3 — Chatting system
*(moved from §14 — chat is part of the playable core, not a post-MLP extra)*
- [ ] Chat Bubble support
- [ ] Chatting UI
- [ ] Private chat (P2P without messages hitting the server they are in) — depends on 8.1's transport; the two items above can land on the existing `LoopbackTransport` path first
**Acceptance criteria:** A player can send chat that others in the lot see as a bubble and in the chat UI, with private chat routed peer-to-peer.
**Difficulty:** 🟠 (bubbles/UI) · ⛔️ private P2P chat (waits on §8.1)

